    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8c0f46ab-70f7-50eb-a388-9d72fb71bbd2",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $6\\mathbf{a} - 2\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda (12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b})$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n6\\mathbf{a} - 2\\mathbf{b}=\\lambda (12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b})=\\lambda (12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b})$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=12\\mathbf{a} - 4\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
